network and talismans </b></li> <li><b>A bomb-maker and trapper who can be a good antagonist for other gamelines</b></li> <li>A Proximus who is able to eat souls and regurgitate them to heal soul loss (She is definitevely appearing in my next Mage game, the concept is neatt)</li> <li>Another star who masquerades her hunt as a reality tv show (could use as a Banisher)</li> <li>A would be superhero prowling the night. (This one is at least an attempt to adress what modern heroes are)</li> <li>A psychatrist seeking to understand the world of dreams (useful as an Hunter antagonist for Astral-focused Mages or Changelings)</li> <li><b>A single-mother house-cleaner using what secrets she discovers to protect her housing block. </b></li> <li>A sailor who hunt Beast on the sea because he perceives their presence as storm noises (Replace Beasts by Magees and you could have an interesting Banisher)</li> <li>A serial killer who genuinely tries to do good.</li> <li>A Hero working for the Cheiron Group</li> </ul><br /> Most of these are sympathetic and it's suggested they could do good or are indeed doing good and just are a danger to the PC's. Which if you do like me and impose on the group not-crappy Hungers could be good.<br /> <br /> Indeed the only outright evil one is the bomb-make. Also interesingly those bolded are gay or bisexual.<br /> <br /> I'll say the section is worth it if only for the soul-eating, soul-healing Proximus (who still heals victims of soul-loss when she sees them) and the youtuber working as an indirect enemies<br /> <br /> Next section are the Beasts, which can be used as antagonists for other lines, they are all eminently punchable<ul><li>An incarnate CEO pushing the firms of Zurich to more and more predatory behaviour</li> <li>A wood-haunting Rampant, nothing to write about</li> <li>A secret hunting Rampant Squid hunting through the Realms Invisible (Who says nice enounter for Mages in the Astral)</li> <li>A water based Incarnate prone to cause storms and sink ships</li> <li>A spider Unfettered punishing those with &amp;quot;dark secrets&amp;quot;</li> <li>A lobbyist tempting those who oppose him to self-destruction</li> <li>A Rampant policing a campus as an urban legen</li> </ul><br /> Then you have the Insatiables. As always there are some good ideas: The Insatiables are basically linked to the elements and their forms are not following human legends (which would be more interesting if most of the RMC had not Horrors not fitting with classic legends). Differences with Beasts include<ul><li>No Astral Lair (although they can steal one from Beasts) but they can create Dens in the material world which they can control like Beasts control their Lairs</li> <li>Elemental associations (Earth, Ice, Sea, Fire, Void)</li> <li>Lovecraftian forms which, unlike Beasts, they can fully summon in the material realm</li> <li>The Schism, some sort of Disquiet which warps the community around the Den in madness and nightmares</li> <li>They must kill to eat and they are always hungry</li> </ul><br /> If you use Beasts as Antagonists, Insatiables have several advantages. They are linked to the material realm and can become huge monsters without going into the Astral. They have this &amp;quot;Primordial Horror&amp;quot; thing primed and yet some are at least subtle to be difficult to find. The Insatiables in the book are<ul><li>A burning mob boss who forces you to fight his cronies even before you get to the &amp;quot;giant lava monster&amp;quot; stage</li> <li>The aforementioned Blind Man, which now I think is meant to emulate the guy from Storm of the Century too, but is the most useless of the bunch</li> <li>An ice girl who devours those who try to help her (Nice but don't scream Primordial Horror to me, that's basically a Yuki-onna)</li> <li>The internet Insatiable, who by the way did not create GG but just has a cult in the same circles (Frankly I fail to see what the problem is. The Scientology is a Banisher Cult in the COD and nobody complains). An interesting take on the &amp;quot;unseen predator&amp;quot;</li> <li>A monster-clown. Well at least it doesn't target children. Nice link though between his sea-assocaition and his habit to drown his prey in a crowd of people.</li> <li>A cannibal everyoung boy who go to school, picks prey and attracts them in an underground place before devouring them. Classic</li> </ul><br /> So in my opinion it's a good Night Horrors books aka a source of antagonists. I cannot say how it compares to other Night Horrors books except it's not Grim Fears (but then Grim Fears was pretty much perfect), at it contains some &amp;quot;meh&amp;quot; monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great detail in your post. You may have have me leaning towards spending some money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:43:09-08:00","id":1031784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031769#post1031769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DrivethruRPG has a Preview option that allows you to see the first few pages. In this book you only see the first part of the Introduction, but it's enough to see the Introduction's quick write-up of the Heroes.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth if anyone who has a say in things is listening, the Introductions to these books are usually incredibly informative, finding a way to have those in the Preview of DTRPG, so far the only way to really get the game, would probably help a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Onyx Path should make sure to have the table of contents and the introduction viewible for free, maybe dtrpg doesn't allow it or aomething. Seems like a no brainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:45:14-08:00","id":1031787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031771#post1031771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankyou this was very helpful. I am interested in the insatiable. How difficult would it be to rebalance them as player options?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not hard. You'd have to take away the Moment bonus, which are really powerful. You wouldn't have to, but you'd probably want to. A lot of their monstrousness is kind of informed. 'They don't care about people,' is easily changed. You could keep the Subverting of Lairs and the Schism, which is similar to Disquiet but less intricate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do Ensurients do? </div> </div> </div>They're kind of like Atavisms, I suppose, most involve their body doing something. They tend towards being really powerful but you could either remove it outright and just give them Atavisms and Nightmares, or tone them down a bit.<br /> <br /> Here's two from the book. This is Cast Aside, 'The Insatiable\u2019s limbs grow suddenly, either becoming massively muscled or bending in ways that maximize his ability to throw others. The Insatiable spends a point of Satiety to let him choose to inflict the Staggered Tilt instead of inflicting damage on a successful melee or brawling attack. The opponent is staggered for one round per damage the Insatiable would have dealt with his attack.'<br /> <br /> And this is Obedience, 'Not all Insatiable like to remain hidden, and some are able to adapt and manipulate mortals into serving their needs. An Insatiable knows that if she operates openly, she is at risk \u2014 not just from Beasts, but also from other supernatural creatures. The Insatiable has developed a means to manipulate humans and get them to act in her stead. Whether it is by releasing pheromones that manipulate their senses or by direct psychic control, the Insatiable is able to use the effects of her Schism to make humans more loyal to her.<br /> Each week an Insatiable may spend 5 points of Satiety minus the Schism\u2019s rating (to a minimum of 1) to force humans who hear her commands to obey her. Humans may roll Resolve + Composure to resist the effects of this power but are at a -1 penalty for each level of the Schism\u2019s rating. The effects of this power last for one week per level of the Schism.'<br /> <br /> If this is posting too much, I can edit it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031784#post1031784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah Onyx Path should make sure to have the table of contents and the introduction viewible for free, maybe dtrpg doesn't allow it or aomething. Seems like a no brainer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Offhand I imagine DTRPG just shows the first 10% of the book, maybe with a cap for larger books. Exalted only shows the first 16 pages, which would be ~2%.<br /> <br /> I think it's more a website thing than an Onyx Path thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-14-2017, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:53:23-08:00","id":1031793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031787#post1031787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not hard. You'd have to take away the Moment bonus, which are really powerful. You wouldn't have to, but you'd probably want to. A lot of their monstrousness is kind of informed. 'They don't care about people,' is easily changed. You could keep the Subverting of Lairs and the Schism, which is similar to Disquiet but less intricate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're kind of like Atavisms, I suppose, most involve their body doing something. They tend towards being really powerful but you could either remove it outright and just give them Atavisms and Nightmares, or tone them down a bit.<br /> <br /> Here's two from the book. This is Cast Aside, 'The Insatiable\u2019s limbs grow suddenly, either becoming massively muscled or bending in ways that maximize his ability to throw others. The Insatiable spends a point of Satiety to let him choose to inflict the Staggered Tilt instead of inflicting damage on a successful melee or brawling attack. The opponent is staggered for one round per damage the Insatiable would have dealt with his attack.'<br /> <br /> And this is Obedience, 'Not all Insatiable like to remain hidden, and some are able to adapt and manipulate mortals into serving their needs. An Insatiable knows that if she operates openly, she is at risk \u2014 not just from Beasts, but also from other supernatural creatures. The Insatiable has developed a means to manipulate humans and get them to act in her stead. Whether it is by releasing pheromones that manipulate their senses or by direct psychic control, the Insatiable is able to use the effects of her Schism to make humans more loyal to her.<br /> Each week an Insatiable may spend 5 points of Satiety minus the Schism\u2019s rating (to a minimum of 1) to force humans who hear her commands to obey her. Humans may roll Resolve + Composure to resist the effects of this power but are at a -1 penalty for each level of the Schism\u2019s rating. The effects of this power last for one week per level of the Schism.'<br /> <br /> If this is posting too much, I can edit it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Offhand I imagine DTRPG just shows the first 10% of the book, maybe with a cap for larger books. Exalted only shows the first 16 pages, which would be ~2%.<br /> <br /> I think it's more a website thing than an Onyx Path thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I like the idea of the atavism-like powers being physical instead of invisible. Well I guess you sold me. Feel free to post as much as you like. I am sure others will find this thread helpful for their buying decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:03:53-08:00","id":1031803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031759#post1031759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you tell me a bit more about their advice on running heroes? Was it a different approach than in the core book? In the core they assumed the heroes were awful people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The advice comes down to giving Heroes a lot of different reasons for doing what they do: fear, torment from the Primordial Dream, glory, inability to stop, etc. Heroes are presented as a bit tragic, in that they Hunger like Beasts, but they can't see their Hunger in any context beyond a certain narrative. The example characters also flesh out what kinds of Heroes Beasts might encounter. Not all of them are horrible people, but none of them are capable of seeing outside their own narrow worldviews. One is a victims' advocate who can't cope with her guilt, and doesn't see that she's being used; one is a serial killer who prefers to channel his urges on Beasts instead of humans (mostly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:06:42-08:00","id":1031806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031766#post1031766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reposted from another forum<br /> <br /> The book is separated in three sections: Heroes, Beasts and the Insatiables.<br /> <br /> The Heroes can easily be restatted as Slashers for an HTV game and include<ul><li>A youtube star who uses her channel to direct other Heroes to Beasts (Internet based Slasher or Hunter anyone)</li> <li><b>A Hunter turned Heroe with a good network and talismans </b></li> <li><b>A bomb-maker and trapper who can be a good antagonist for other gamelines</b></li> <li>A Proximus who is able to eat souls and regurgitate them to heal soul loss (She is definitevely appearing in my next Mage game, the concept is neatt)</li> <li>Another star who masquerades her hunt as a reality tv show (could use as a Banisher)</li> <li>A would be superhero prowling the night. (This one is at least an attempt to adress what modern heroes are)</li> <li>A psychatrist seeking to understand the world of dreams (useful as an Hunter antagonist for Astral-focused Mages or Changelings)</li> <li><b>A single-mother house-cleaner using what secrets she discovers to protect her housing block. </b></li> <li>A sailor who hunt Beast on the sea because he perceives their presence as storm noises (Replace Beasts by Magees and you could have an interesting Banisher)</li> <li>A serial killer who genuinely tries to do good.</li> <li>A Hero working for the Cheiron Group</li> </ul><br /> Most of these are sympathetic and it's suggested they could do good or are indeed doing good and just are a danger to the PC's. Which if you do like me and impose on the group not-crappy Hungers could be good.<br /> <br /> <br /> So in my opinion it's a good Night Horrors books aka a source of antagonists. I cannot say how it compares to other Night Horrors books except it's not Grim Fears (but then Grim Fears was pretty much perfect), at it contains some &quot;meh&quot; monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've just sold me on the book. I'm someone who likes the Heroes concept even more than the Beasts, so this book would be right up my alley. Especially since I think it could get a TON of use in a Hunter the Vigil game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:35:22-08:00","id":1031848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031803#post1031803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The advice comes down to giving Heroes a lot of different reasons for doing what they do: fear, torment from the Primordial Dream, glory, inability to stop, etc. Heroes are presented as a bit tragic, in that they Hunger like Beasts, but they can't see their Hunger in any context beyond a certain narrative. The example characters also flesh out what kinds of Heroes Beasts might encounter. Not all of them are horrible people, but none of them are capable of seeing outside their own narrow worldviews. One is a victims' advocate who can't cope with her guilt, and doesn't see that she's being used; one is a serial killer who prefers to channel his urges on Beasts instead of humans (mostly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like I need to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:40:21-08:00","id":1031852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031806#post1031806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you've just sold me on the book. I'm someone who likes the Heroes concept even more than the Beasts, so this book would be right up my alley. Especially since I think it could get a TON of use in a Hunter the Vigil game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is some good discussion as to how Heroes work with Hunters. This book really swung me over to liking the released Heroes, opposed to the Heroes given in the Kickstarter preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T18:25:29-08:00","id":1031907,"title":"","content":"I'd add that in addition, it really presents Heroes as very human antagonists. Each with their own sympathies and flaws. Which dovetails nicely with my favorite section of the book, the Antagonist Beast section.<br /> <br /> Not only does it present more clear reasons why Beasts come into conflict, but also gives fantastic examples of what you can to with Rampant, Unfettered, and Incarnate Beasts. It also hints that the Inheritance might not be as beneficent for Beasts as some would believe, since even the Incarnate Beast becomes something fully inhuman compared to how the Begotten exist as both humans and nightmares. <br /> <br /> The Insatiable are fantastic too in my opinion since they represent a Strix-like antagonist for the Begotten and...well, anyone they can get their mouths around really. If Beasts represent humanity's own fears and how they can grow from them, then the Insatiable represent cosmic indifference that has no moral beyond existence is cruel and unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T19:52:34-08:00","id":1031938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031907#post1031907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd add that in addition, it really presents Heroes as very human antagonists. Each with their own sympathies and flaws. Which dovetails nicely with my favorite section of the book, the Antagonist Beast section.<br /> <br /> Not only does it present more clear reasons why Beasts come into conflict, but also gives fantastic examples of what you can to with Rampant, Unfettered, and Incarnate Beasts. It also hints that the Inheritance might not be as beneficent for Beasts as some would believe, since even the Incarnate Beast becomes something fully inhuman compared to how the Begotten exist as both humans and nightmares.<br /> <br /> The Insatiable are fantastic too in my opinion since they represent a Strix-like antagonist for the Begotten and...well, anyone they can get their mouths around really. If Beasts represent humanity's own fears and how they can grow from them, then the Insatiable represent cosmic indifference that has no moral beyond existence is cruel and unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovecraft? So were they human like beast, or were they never human, and if so why do they take on human form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T20:37:27-08:00","id":1031959,"title":"","content":"So heroes have been fleshed out a bit more with the book, but I have to ask have they been made more threatening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T20:39:34-08:00","id":1031960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031938#post1031938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So were they human like beast, or were they never human, and if so why do they take on human form?</div> </div> </div> </div>They take on human form because they've effectively consumed the soul of one as part of the fundament of humanity's nightmares.<br /> <br /> If there's one thing the Insatiables do fairly unambiguously, it's underline why the gameline's title characters are &quot;beasts&quot; \u2014 the Begotten bear influence over the Primordial Dream because they are hungry and horrifying creatures whose environment suits their needs; the Insatiable bear influence over the Primordial Dream because they are <i>hungry and horrifying environments</i>.<br /> <br /> Should the world itself turn upside-down, you can avoid the horror of the manticore once placed in its company, but you cannot avoid the horror of the lonely places of the earth \u2014 each Moment is an apocalyptic scenario with no way out, and it is this directionless panic that the Insatiable inflict upon their victims in the process of consuming them entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T21:39:53-08:00","id":1031979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031938#post1031938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovecraft? So were they human like beast, or were they never human, and if so why do they take on human form?</div> </div> </div> </div>At first glance they're almost indistinguishable from Beasts, but that's the Lovecraft angle coming through.<br /> <br /> They have human forms like Beasts, and were once humans themselves before being consumed by their Moment, their equivelent of a Horror. Unlike the Begotten though, the Insatiable are parasitic and can only manifest in individuals who already have connections to the Primordial Dream but have not become Beasts or Heroes. And, also unlike Beast they have absolutely no vestige of their former humanity after their creation. If a Beast must define their life by having to live with their Hunger, then the Insatiable must define their life as their hunger.<br /> <br /> The reason they must take human forms is because for reasons lost to time the Primordial Dream rejects then, and they can only gain Satiaety by physically killing creatures and feeding off their fear (mostly of the time.) They have no Lair of their own, an must create shallow Dens in the waking world, but can hyjack the Lair of a Beast so long as they remain alive in order to steal their might an powers (Lair rating and Atavisms.)<br /> <br /> Their unknown rejection from the Primordial Dream also means they interact with it in strange ways. When they feed, unlike Beasts, the fears of humanity don't get filtered back into the Primordial Dream but this also means they cause virtually no ripples through their predations for Heroes and Beasts to pick up from the Primordial Dream. They do however cause quite the waves in the waking world by disrupting human's connection to the Primordial Dream by an effect called Schism. It's not to different from a Promethean's Disquiet except that it can be greatly benificial to the Insatiable at the cost of alerting canny observer's to it's presence. It also subsides once the Insatiable moves on as the Primordial Dream repairs itself, but the longer they stay and feed in one place the worse it gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T21:44:24-08:00","id":1031980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031960#post1031960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They take on human form because they've effectively consumed the soul of one as part of the fundament of humanity's nightmares.<br /> <br /> If there's one thing the Insatiables do fairly unambiguously, it's underline why the gameline's title characters are &amp;quot;beasts&amp;quot; \u2014 the Begotten bear influence over the Primordial Dream because they are hungry and horrifying creatures whose environment suits their needs; the Insatiable bear influence over the Primordial Dream because they are <i>hungry and horrifying environments</i>.<br /> <br /> Should the world itself turn upside-down, you can avoid the horror of the manticore once placed in its company, but you cannot avoid the horror of the lonely places of the earth \u2014 each Moment is an apocalyptic scenario with no way out, and it is this directionless panic that the Insatiable inflict upon their victims in the process of consuming them entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that ^<br /> <br /> That was much more well presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:49:18-08:00","id":1032000,"title":"","content":"Welp, I learned a lot thanks all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:56:27-08:00","id":1032254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031803#post1031803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> one is a serial killer who prefers to channel his urges on Beasts instead of humans (mostly).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of getting a Dexter Vibe from that one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:11:47-08:00","id":1032261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031959#post1031959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So heroes have been fleshed out a bit more with the book, but I have to ask have they been made more threatening?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a couple new Gifts that are pretty potent, and the new Anathema is horrifying. Not a lot has been added mechanically, but you get a better sense of how they can be effective. I mean, Heroes can be very dangerous, it's just that they need followers or resources, and to be able to place Anathema. Hunt smart, not often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:41:31-08:00","id":1032268,"title":"","content":"It has a killer clown.<br /> <br /> I mean that would be enough for me, but YMMV <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T15:04:07-08:00","id":1032343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1031959#post1031959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So heroes have been fleshed out a bit more with the book, but I have to ask have they been made more threatening?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit curious on this. Why do you think Heroes aren't threatening enough already?<br /> <br /> I mean, are there any particular areas you think they're underperforming in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:45:07-08:00","id":1032730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1032343#post1032343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a bit curious on this. Why do you think Heroes aren't threatening enough already?<br /> <br /> I mean, are there any particular areas you think they're underperforming in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno, it was the first thing my ST asked when I mentioned it* and I recall a few people saying they felt Heroes weren't as dangerous as they should be. Thus I felt it was a fair question to ask if they still felt that way to some with the new book.<br /> <br /> <br /> *It also doesn't help that I just found out he missed the section in the book covering mechanical benefits to Heroes, so he was unaware of any of their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:36:54-08:00","id":1032759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1032730#post1032730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *It also doesn't help that I just found out he missed the section in the book covering mechanical benefits to Heroes, so he was unaware of any of their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'mma fight Godzilla!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...how?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Grit!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:36:06-08:00","id":1032842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031726-sell-me-on-conqurering-heroes?p=1032730#post1032730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno, it was the first thing my ST asked when I mentioned it* and I recall a few people saying they felt Heroes weren't as dangerous as they should be. Thus I felt it was a fair question to ask if they still felt that way to some with the new book.<br /> <br /> <br /> *It also doesn't help that I just found out he missed the section in the book covering mechanical benefits to Heroes, so he was unaware of any of their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, gotcha. Thanks!<br /> <br /> The thing that really took me by surprise... Is learning that an aggressive Hero has a strong change of regaining ALL of their Willpower back just for daring to fight you as a Beast. Willpower can really swing fights and part of the defense of a Beast's Lair is that working your way through Burrows is meant to drain Willpower. But Heroes? They get it all back when they're facing off the REAL threat of the Lair....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:49:17-08:00","id":1032893,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking it's still very easy for a Beast to outmatch a Hero in direct combat. The strengths of their respective powers, and the ease with which said powers are acquired/applied tilt heavily in favor of Beasts, but Conquering Heroes does a really good job of showcasing Heroes who use smarter tactics to create a significant threat. The ones that turn social networks against the player characters are particularly nasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}